<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments rise in Oct month-on-month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments rise in Oct month-on-month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by banks in Kuwait to finance imports rose to 134 million dinars in October from 116 million in September, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 145.1 million dinars in October 1995.</p>
<p>				  Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>				     Oct '96     Sept '96   Oct '95</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   90.6	  81.4	104.6</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    18.6	  17.4	 21.7</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    24.9	  17.2	 18.8</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing fell to 60.3 percent in October from 64.3 in September. That of the Japanese yen rose to 5.5 percent from 5.1 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.302 dinar)</p>
</text>
